index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..f2e86e4586112f42bebfe1c02f2d7c5ca72751ea
--- /dev/null
+++ b/skills/gemini-delegate/SKILL.md
@@ -0,0 +1,90 @@
+---
+name: gemini-delegate
+description: >-
+  Delegate a coding task to Gemini CLI (`gemini`) as a background implementer, then
+  review its diff and land it yourself. Use when the user wants to delegate implementation
+  work to Gemini - "have Gemini implement X", "delegate this to gemini", "run it through
+  Gemini", or "use Gemini to implement/fix/refactor" - or run a queue of coding tasks
+  through Gemini while staying the reviewer. DO NOT USE for tasks small enough to do
+  inline, or when the user wants code written directly without delegating.
+license: MIT
+compatibility: Requires Gemini CLI (`gemini`) installed and authenticated through its interactive `gemini` sign-in or its configured provider, Node 18+, and git. The orchestrator must run shell commands and read files.
+metadata:
+  version: 0.5.0
+---
+
+# Gemini Delegate
+
+You are the **orchestrator**. Send a bounded, self-contained **brief** to Gemini CLI as
+a separate **implementer**, review its working-tree diff, run the project's **gates**,
+then **land** the work yourself. The relay never commits.
+
+## Prerequisites
+
+- Have `gemini` installed on PATH and authenticate through interactive `gemini` or
+  the CLI's configured provider. The relay inherits that configuration; it does not
+  read or write credentials.
+- Confirm `gemini --version` and inspect `gemini --help` for the documented flags.
+- Use a clean target git repository or isolated worktree. Brief scope is guidance,
+  not containment; do not delegate irreversible or sensitive operations without approval.
+
+## Model selection (optional)
+
+Omit `--model` to preserve the CLI's own Auto/default behavior. An explicit
+`--model <id>` or saved lane model is optional; no model pin is required. Use a
+model identifier your CLI supports, not a guessed catalog. Tokens accept letters,
+digits, and `. _ : / -` because argv reaches an npm `.cmd` shim on Windows.
+
+## The loop
+
+1. **Write a brief** with the goal, allowed scope, exclusions, real gates, and a
+   closing report contract. Gemini cannot see the orchestrator's chat history.
+   Read [writing-the-brief.md](references/writing-the-brief.md).
+2. **Dispatch** using the bundled relay, preferably with the orchestrator's
+   background-command facility:
+
+   ```bash
+   node "<skill-dir>/scripts/relay.mjs" --brief brief.txt --cd /path/to/repo
+   # saved lane:          add --lane feature
+   # optional model:      add --model <id>
+   # planning request:    add --approval-mode plan (not a read-only guarantee)
+   # all-tool approval:   add --approval-mode yolo (explicit full trust)
+   # resume:              add --resume <index> or --resume-last, with a delta brief
+   # longer watchdog:     add --timeout 2h (default: 30m)
+   ```
+
+   `<skill-dir>` contains this skill's `SKILL.md`. The child cwd sets the workspace;
+   the brief stays on stdin behind a fixed headless `--prompt`. Native Windows
+   launches the npm `.cmd` shim with `shell:true`, keeping brief and paths out of argv.
+3. **Wait** for the relay to exit and read its atomic `result.json`, not progress text.
+   See [dispatch-and-poll.md](references/dispatch-and-poll.md) for the result contract.
+4. **Review** the diff against the brief and independently re-run the gates. A
+   success event is not proof of a correct implementation. See
+   [review-and-land.md](references/review-and-land.md).
+5. **Land** only verified work, when authorized. Otherwise resume with a narrow
+   correction brief and review again. For queues, read
+   [multi-task-queues.md](references/multi-task-queues.md).
+
+## Approval modes and limits
+
+The relay defaults to `--approval-mode auto_edit`, which auto-approves edit tools,
+not all shell actions. `default` prompts for approvals; approval-required actions
+may be unavailable in a headless run. `yolo` auto-approves all tools and must be
+explicitly selected or present in an approved lane. No mode is an OS sandbox.
+
+Gemini calls `plan` read-only in its help, but CLI settings can disable plan and
+downgrade it to `default`. The relay therefore exposes the exact `--approval-mode`
+without a `--read-only` alias or `readOnly` lane dial. It does not configure sandbox,
+policy, extensions, hooks, MCP, or workspace trust bypasses. Inherited CLI settings
+and project instructions still apply. Do not use this skill when an enforced
+read-only boundary is required; use OS-enforced isolation instead.
+
+Saved Gemini lanes support `model`, `permissionMode` (mapped to `--approval-mode`),
+and `timeout`. Explicit flags win. Discovery probes only `gemini --version`;
+authentication, model catalog, and usage remain unknown rather than guessed.
+
+## Verification
+
+Contract-tested with a fake CLI; no live model dispatch is recorded. Offline CLI
+help/version and installed-source inspection ground the launch and stream fields.
+Neither headless write approval nor plan-mode containment has been live-tested.
