@@ -0,0 +1,95 @@
+# Dispatch and poll
+
+```bash
+node "<skill-dir>/scripts/relay.mjs" --brief brief.txt --cd /path/to/repo
+```
+
+## Flags and launch
+
+| Relay flag | Effect |
+| --- | --- |
+| `--brief <file>` | Read the brief from a file; omitted means relay stdin. |
+| `--cd <dir>` | Child cwd; default current directory. |
+| `--lane <name>` | Resolve an approved fleet lane for `gemini`; explicit dials win. |
+| `--model <id>` | Optional explicit model. Omit to keep Gemini Auto/default. Shell-safe token. |
+| `--approval-mode <mode>` | `default`, `auto_edit`, `yolo`, `plan`; default `auto_edit`. |
+| `--resume <selector>` | `latest` or a positive index from `gemini --list-sessions` in the target project. |
+| `--resume-last` | Alias for `--resume latest`; conflicts with `--resume`. |
+| `--timeout <dur>` | Relay watchdog, default `30m`; positive h/m/s duration up to ~24.8 days. |
+| `--out-dir <dir>` | Run artifacts; default a fresh system-temp directory. |
+| `-h`, `--help` | Relay help; no dispatch. |
+
+The launch is equivalent to this command **in the target directory**:
+
+```bash
+gemini --output-format stream-json --approval-mode auto_edit \
+  --prompt "Follow the task instructions provided on stdin." < brief.txt
+# optional: --model <id>, --resume <selector>, or a different --approval-mode
+```
+
+The prompt is appended to stdin by Gemini. Native Windows resolves `gemini.cmd`
+through `shell:true`; the fixed prompt is quoted and dynamic argv is token-validated.
+The brief and cwd never reach shell argv. No trust/sandbox/policy flags are added.
+`auto_edit` does not grant every shell action; `yolo` grants all-tool approval, not
+workspace containment. Plan can be downgraded by settings and is not enforced as
+read-only by this relay. Approval mode in the result is the **requested** mode.
+
+Resume selectors are intentionally limited to the help-documented latest/index
+forms. `sessionId` is captured for diagnostics, not accepted as a relay resume flag.
+Gemini may start a new session when `latest` finds none; `resumed` records the
+request, not proof that earlier context was loaded.
+
+## Result contract and artifacts
+
+Artifacts: exact `brief.txt`, raw stdout `events.jsonl`, complete `stderr.txt`,
+`final.txt` when assistant text exists, and atomic `result.json`. Reusing an
+`--out-dir` clears old final/result files and truncates event/stderr logs. Keep
+artifacts outside the worktree if they should not appear in `touchedFiles`.
+
+`result.json` speaks `delegate-relay.result.v1`:
+
+- `schema`, `tool: "gemini"`, `status` (`completed`, `failed`, `timeout`, `aborted`,
+  `gemini_unavailable`), `exitCode`, nullable `signal`.
+- `workdir`, nullable requested `model`, requested `approvalMode`, nullable
+  `resume`, request boolean `resumed`, nullable `lane` and `laneSource`.
+- `geminiVersion`, `startedAt`, `finishedAt`, artifact paths `briefPath`,
+  `eventsPath`, `stderrPath`, and nullable `finalPath`.
+- Nullable `sessionId` and `initialModel` from the `init` event's `session_id`
+  and `model`. The initial model may be an Auto alias, not the final routed model.
+- Nullable `resultStatus` and `stats` from the `result` event. Stats are retained
+  as Gemini emits them, not synthesized as billing or a model catalog.
+- `finalMessage`: joined assistant `message.content` text, including streamed
+  deltas. It can include intermediate narration; user/tool text is excluded.
+- `touchedFiles`: final `git status --porcelain` lines under `--cd`. `[]` means
+  clean, `null` means Git could not report. Pre-existing dirt is included; this
+  is not attribution, and cannot show ignored files, reverted edits, or writes
+  outside the repository.
+- `error` on failure; `stderrTail` holds up to 20 non-empty lines of the retained
+  stderr suffix. Complete diagnostics remain in `stderr.txt` and `events.jsonl`.
+
+Completion requires child exit 0 and a `result.status: "success"`, with no
+error-severity stream event. Missing/malformed result, error result, error-severity
+event, or non-zero exit fails. Warning events and recovered tool errors are not
+alone fatal; review the event log and diff for unmet requirements.
+
+## Waiting and failures
+
+Run in the orchestrator's background-command facility and wait for the process
+to finish. Poll `result.json` if needed; it is published by an atomic rename.
+
+- Usage errors exit **2**, before creating artifacts or a result.
+- Missing `gemini` exits **127** with `gemini_unavailable` and nullable final path.
+- A bounded `--version` preflight (10s cap, limited by `--timeout`) runs before
+  dispatch. Failed version exits preserve a non-zero CLI code; a hung preflight
+  reports `timeout`/124 and says dispatch did not start.
+- A failed dispatch preserves non-zero child exits; a zero exit with a failed
+  stream maps to 1. Signal exits map to 128 plus the signal number.
+- Watchdog timeouts kill the whole process tree (POSIX process group with a 10s
+  escalation, native Windows `taskkill /t /f`) and cannot report completed even
+  if the child exits 0 during shutdown. Inspect partial edits before retrying.
+- Catchable relay signals write `aborted` and forward termination; the final Git
+  snapshot is refreshed after the shutdown grace. Native Windows hard kills
+  are uncatchable and may leave no result: inspect the tree and logs directly.
+
+No live Gemini dispatch is recorded. Contract tests cover the transport and event
+contract, not model correctness, trust/approval policy, or enforced read-only behavior.
