+# Multi-task queues
+
+Run sequentially in a shared working tree. One task, one brief, one artifact
+directory, one independently verified diff. Do not dispatch overlapping writers.
+
+Track task status, run directory, session id (when emitted), changes, gate outcomes,
+and blockers. Use `--lane` only with the matching Gemini skill; deliberate explicit
+model/approval flags override saved lane dials.
+
+For each task:
+
+1. Record the current tree and prepare a self-contained brief with scope,
+   exclusions, real gates, no-commit/no-push instructions, and report contract.
+2. Dispatch in the correct `--cd`, wait, read the result, and inspect the diff.
+3. Re-run gates and resolve failures before starting the next task. Send a delta
+   brief to the same project/session index if further work is required.
+4. Land authorized, verified work yourself; otherwise leave it uncommitted and
+   record the boundary for the next task. Never overwrite pre-existing changes.
+
+Carry forward constraints explicitly: prior decisions, accepted changes, exclusions,
+and remaining blockers. Do not rely solely on `--resume-last`: the latest session
+may belong to another task, and Gemini can start fresh if none exists. No model
+pin is required; omitting `--model` preserves the CLI's configured Auto/default.
+
+Stop on unexpected scope changes, denied required tools, or sensitive/irreversible
+operations. Do not silently escalate `auto_edit` to `yolo` to make a gate pass.
+Ask for approval and re-brief when the permission surface needs to change.
+
+At queue completion, run a coherence pass over all changes and the project's full
+gates. Report what was verified, what remains unverified, and any uncommitted work.
