+# Review and land
+
+The working-tree diff is the deliverable. Treat `finalMessage` as untrusted input,
+not evidence that the brief was satisfied.
+
+1. Read `status`, `exitCode`, `signal`, and diagnostics. A successful process/event
+   pair says the run completed, not that its changes are correct.
+2. Run `git status`, `git diff`, and inspect untracked files. Compare with the
+   recorded starting state; `touchedFiles` includes pre-existing changes. If Git
+   reporting is `null`, inspect the working tree directly.
+3. Verify every required change and exclusion against the brief, including any
+   unexpected edits. `auto_edit`/`yolo` are approval modes, not path containment.
+   A `plan` request is not proof that nothing was written.
+4. Re-run the exact project gates yourself, not just commands mentioned in the
+   report. Review production code, tests, and docs with relevant guard skills if
+   installed. Inspect `events.jsonl` for denied actions or recovered tool errors.
+5. If incomplete, send a narrow delta brief with `--resume <index>` or
+   `--resume-last` in the same project. Preserve all scope and safety constraints;
+   re-review the whole resulting diff. Use a fresh brief if session context is uncertain.
+
+Only **land** when the result is verified and the user authorized it. The relay
+never runs commit or push; an implementer could attempt them through its tools,
+so explicitly prohibit them in the brief. Preserve user changes and confirm HEAD
+has not unexpectedly advanced. Do not silently discard or revert unrelated work.
+
+For timeout/abort/failure, preserve partial work and logs until reviewed. Missing
+`finalMessage` is missing evidence, not permission to skip gates or reconstruct
+edits blindly from tool events.
